---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import CopyBlock from '../components/CopyBlock.astro';
import { toolFamilies, marketplace } from '../data/tools';
---

<Layout
  title="ExFu agent tools & setup"
  description="Explore ExFu plugins, add the marketplace and follow setup instructions for the tool you choose. Help for Cowork and Claude Code users."
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow red">ExFu agent tools</p><h1>
        Tools for agents.<br />Help getting started.
      </h1><p class="lead tools-lead">
        Explore the plugins, choose what would help, and get it working. Everything you need to
        start is below.
      </p><a class="button" href={marketplace}>Explore the full marketplace ↗</a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <div class="wrap tools-layout">
    <nav class="tools-sidebar" aria-label="Tools page sections">
      <p class="eyebrow">On this page</p><a href="#tool-catalogue">Explore the tools</a><a
        href="#marketplace">1. Add the marketplace</a
      ><a href="#setup">2. Choose & install</a><a href="#first-session">3. First session</a><a
        href="#troubleshooting">Get unstuck</a
      >
    </nav>
    <div class="tools-main">
      <section id="tool-catalogue" class="tools-chapter">
        <p class="eyebrow red">Find your starting point</p><h2>What would help your agent?</h2><p>
          These are a few of the main plugins. The <a href={marketplace}>marketplace</a> often has more
          tools and editions than we list here, along with their current documentation.
        </p><div class="tools-choices">
          {
            toolFamilies.map((tool) => (
              <article>
                <>
                  <h3>{tool.name}</h3>
                  <p>{tool.description}</p>
                  <a href="#setup" data-choose-plugin={tool.pkg} class="text-link">
                    Set up this plugin ↗
                  </a>
                </>
              </article>
            ))
          }<article class="more-tools">
            <h3>And more</h3><p>
              See what else is available, including other editions and new additions.
            </p><a class="text-link" href={marketplace}>Browse the marketplace ↗</a>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section id="marketplace" class="tools-chapter">
        <p class="eyebrow red">Step 1 · Once per app</p><h2>Add the ExFu marketplace.</h2><p>
          The marketplace is the catalogue Claude uses to find ExFu plugins. Add it once, then
          choose whichever plugins you want. If you have already added it, <a href="#setup"
            >go straight to your plugin</a
          >.
        </p><div class="setup-options">
          <article class="setup-option">
            <h3>In Cowork</h3><p>
              In Claude Desktop, open Cowork, then <strong>Customize → Plugins</strong>. Under
              Personal plugins, choose <strong>+ → Add marketplace</strong> and add from a repository.
            </p><CopyBlock text={marketplace} label="Copy marketplace address" /><a
              href="https://support.claude.com/en/articles/13837440-use-plugins-in-claude"
              >Claude’s plugin guide ↗</a
            >
          </article><article class="setup-option">
            <h3>In Claude Code</h3><p>
              With Claude Code installed and signed in, paste this into your terminal:
            </p><CopyBlock
              text="claude plugin marketplace add ExFu/exfu-marketplace"
              label="Copy terminal marketplace command"
            /><p>Or, inside a Claude Code conversation:</p><CopyBlock
              text="/plugin marketplace add ExFu/exfu-marketplace"
              label="Copy conversation marketplace command"
            /><a href="https://code.claude.com/docs/en/discover-plugins"
              >Claude Code plugin guide ↗</a
            >
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section id="setup" class="tools-chapter plugin-workspace">
        <div class="plugin-picker" hidden>
          <p class="eyebrow red">Step 2 · Your chosen plugin</p><label for="plugin-choice"
            >What are we installing?</label
          ><select id="plugin-choice"
            >{toolFamilies.map((tool) => <option value={tool.pkg}>{tool.name}</option>)}</select
          ><p id="plugin-selection-status" role="status">Showing Agent Library instructions.</p>
        </div><div class="selected-plugin-body">
          <h2 id="selected-tool-title">Install the Agent Library.</h2><p
            id="selected-plugin-description"
          >
            {toolFamilies[0].detail}
          </p><p>Marketplace added? These instructions install just this plugin.</p><div
            class="setup-options"
          >
            <article class="setup-option">
              <h3>In Cowork</h3><p>
                Browse your ExFu marketplace and find <strong id="selected-plugin-name"
                  >exfu-agent-library-solo</strong
                >. Choose Install, then check that it is enabled.
              </p>
            </article><article class="setup-option">
              <h3>In Claude Code</h3><p>In your terminal:</p><div id="selected-terminal">
                <CopyBlock
                  text="claude plugin install exfu-agent-library-solo@exfu-marketplace"
                  label="Copy Agent Library install command"
                />
              </div><p>Or in a Claude Code conversation:</p><CopyBlock
                text="/plugin install exfu-agent-library-solo@exfu-marketplace"
                id="selected-slash"
              />
            </article>
          </div>
          <section id="first-session" class="setup-next">
            <p class="eyebrow red">Step 3 · Try your chosen plugin</p><p>
              Start a fresh session. If the plugin has not appeared, restart Claude and check that
              it is enabled.
            </p>{
              toolFamilies.map((tool, i) => (
                <div data-plugin-first={tool.pkg} hidden={i !== 0}>
                  <>
                    <h3>{tool.setupTitle}</h3>
                    <p>{tool.preparation}</p>
                    <p>Paste this to begin:</p>
                    <CopyBlock text={tool.setupPrompt} label={`Copy ${tool.name} setup prompt`} />
                    <p>{tool.setupNote}</p>
                  </>
                </div>
              ))
            }
          </section>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section id="troubleshooting" class="tools-chapter">
        <p class="eyebrow red">A little support</p><h2>Something not working?</h2><article
          class="faq-answer"
        >
          <h3>I can’t find the plugin.</h3><p>
            Check that the ExFu marketplace was added in the app you are using, and the plugin is
            installed and enabled. On a managed work account, your administrator may need to allow
            it.
          </p>
        </article><article class="faq-answer">
          <h3>Claude doesn’t recognise the setup.</h3><p>
            Start a new session in the app where you installed the plugin. Select your working
            folder and ask whether Claude can see the plugin’s skills. If not, restart the app and
            check your installed plugins.
          </p>
        </article><div class="tools-help">
          <h3>Still stuck?</h3><p>
            Email <a href="mailto:al@exfu.ai">al@exfu.ai</a> with the app you’re using, the step you reached
            and the error message. Leave out passwords and private client information.
          </p><a class="text-link" href="/personal-support/">Prefer to get set up together? ↗</a>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div><script src="../scripts/tool-setup.ts"></script></Layout
>
